---
import Card from "astro-theme-university/components/Card.astro";
import CardGrid from "astro-theme-university/components/CardGrid.astro";
import ContentLayout from "astro-theme-university/layouts/ContentLayout.astro";
import heroImage from "../assets/images/hero-home.jpg";
import { courseMeta } from "../course-config";
import { sessionLabels, siteConfig } from "../site-config";
---

<ContentLayout
  title={`${courseMeta.code}: ${courseMeta.title}`}
  description={courseMeta.description}
  heroImage={heroImage}
  heroImageAlt="An illustrated campus corridor: students cluster in conversation past lockers and lecture-hall doors, while near the entrance two students staff a pop-up stall labelled HALLWAY ECONOMICS, handing a zine to a passer-by"
  {...siteConfig}
>
  <ul class="course-tags" aria-label="Course tags">
    {courseMeta.tags.map((tag) => <li>{tag}</li>)}
  </ul>

  <h2>What you will do</h2>
  <p>
    You start conversations with strangers, trade favours, and run a stall
    to see who stops — then work up to asking for something you might be
    turned down for. Each of these is a Crossing: two weeks, one out in the
    hallway and one back reporting what happened, ending with a reflection
    and a short video clip. The last Crossing is built the same way — you
    leave something behind in the hallway, then present your whole
    semester. What you walk out with: a written record of six real
    interactions, and one video, built one clip at a time.
  </p>

  <h2>Who it is for</h2>
  <p>
    Anyone who wants to get better at hearing no, meeting people they
    wouldn't otherwise talk to, and noticing what's already around them on
    campus. No portfolio, no pitch deck, no prior networking experience —
    just a willingness to walk up to someone and start something. If the
    idea of setting up a stall in the busiest foyer on campus makes you
    wince a little — good, this is the course for you. If you don't want
    to consistently try and reflect, it's not for you.
  </p>

  <h2>Where to go next</h2>
  <CardGrid columns={2}>
    <Card title={sessionLabels.plural} href="/sessions/">
      <p>The weekly fieldwork brief: what you do out in the hallway, and how you report it back.</p>
    </Card>
    <Card title="Assessment" href="/assessments/">
      <p>What is marked, what it is worth, and when it is due.</p>
    </Card>
    <Card title="People" href="/people/">
      <p>Who teaches the course and how to reach them.</p>
    </Card>
  </CardGrid>
</ContentLayout>

<style>
  .course-tags {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 0.5rem;
    margin-block: 0 2rem;
    padding: 0;
    list-style: none;
  }

  .course-tags li {
    padding: 0.25rem 0.65rem;
    border-radius: 999px;
    color: var(--at-text-secondary);
    background: var(--at-bg-alt);
    font-size: 0.9rem;
  }
</style>
